            <ArticleTitle>Clinical intestinal gas syndromes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>621-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Belching, flatulence, abdominal distention, and gas pains are common symptoms that may stimulate concern for the patient and from the physician. An understanding of the pathophysiology of intestinal gas syndromes should permit a more focused diagnostic and therapeutic approach.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
